<p>The following formulas describe vertical upward motion:</p>

<p>Velocity in the direction of the y-axis: <strong>v<sub>0Y</sub> = v<sub>0</sub> * sin(a) - g * t</strong></p>

<p>Displacement along the y-axis: <strong>y = v<sub>0</sub> * t - g * t² / 2</strong></p>

<p>Time required to reach the highest point of the trajectory: <strong>t = v<sub>0</sub> / g</strong></p>

<p>Maximum height reached: <strong>H<sub>Max</sub> = v<sub>0</sub>² / (2 * g)</strong></p>
